WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.140
If there's one thing Rick and Morty loves,
it's unorthodox crossover promotions.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:04.720
The Adult Swim series has done a number of
unexpected ads for a variety of media.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.740
They generally consist of the titular characters
not taking the promotion seriously and going

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.280
off on a tangent that makes you, the viewer,
question why whatever company they're promoting

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.940
thought the ad would be a good idea.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.580
Like, for example, the Rick and Morty ad for
Alien: Covenant, which devolved into an argument

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.880
between Rick and Morty about, uhh… drinking
drugs.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.240
"You know, I never thought I'd say this, but
thank God you drink all those drugs and alcohol,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:27.740
y'know?"

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.600
"Morty, you don't drink drugs."

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.160
"Well, whatever.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:29.940
I don't know.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:30.520
I'm innocent."

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.400
Still, the ads must provide some kind of good
buzz, because a new, bizarre mashup has arrived:

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.360
Rick and Morty meets Death Stranding.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.820
In the 30-second spot, Rick and Morty are
seen walking through an animated version of

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.080
the landscape of Death Stranding, the highly-anticipated
PS4 game developed by Kojima Productions.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.560
Rick looks like his normal self, while Morty
is dressed like the protagonist from the soon-to-be-released

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.920
game — Norman Reedus' Sam Porter Bridges
– complete with a floating baby in a tank

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:56.740
on his chest.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.060
Yeah, it's a weird game.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.000
Rick remarks that Hideo Kojima — the writer,
director, designer, and producer of Death

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.030
Stranding – has enlisted their help to try
to repair the game's dystopian world.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.260
"What are these ghosts?"

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.820
"Uh, those are the Death Stranding, Rick."

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.500
"Oh, OK, yeah…

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.240
I wasn't paying attention."

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.600
Eventually, the duo's attention turns to the
baby as they try and decipher its purpose.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.760
Is it an upgrade?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.200
Some sort of health potion?

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.220
In the end, they decide to take the only logical
action:

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:22.920
"Let's eat it!"

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:23.820
"We can't eat it.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.320
It's a baby."

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.380
"Morty, what if it makes us run faster or
jump higher?"

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.340
".......OK, let's eat the baby."

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.080
Yeah, it's a seriously twisted ad for an equally
bonkers kind of video game.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:37.689
At first glance, a Rick and Morty and Death
Stranding crossover may feel like an odd match.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:41.979
After all, one is an animated comedy series
that doesn't take itself too seriously while

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.810
the other is a dramatic video game that takes
itself extremely seriously.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.119
But when you think about it, these two properties
actually go together pretty well — and not

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:52.010
just because of their sci-fi connections.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.140
Rather, it's because they're both really weird.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.100
Rick and Morty is pretty mainstream.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.480
It's probably the most popular Adult Swim
series ever, and it has one of the most dedicated

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.390
fanbases of any show currently on television.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.210
Every time a new Rick and Morty season is
announced, it's basically treated like an

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.600
event, and few other shows can match the excitement
it generates.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.060
With the series' popularity, it's easy to
forget just how strange Rick and Morty is.

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:19.120
This is a show that has turned its protagonist
into a pickle, featured a character named

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.480
Mr. Poopybutthole, and woven a complex serialized
narrative that involves a multiverse and lots

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.820
of nonsensical — but strangely believable
— sci-fi jargon.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.060
Pretty much the only current, mainstream piece
of entertainment that surpasses Rick and Morty

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.860
in weirdness is Death Stranding.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.600
Seemingly no one can adequately describe what
the game is about – its ludicrously complex

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:43.080
story involves a post-apocalyptic America,
invisible ghosts, babies in jars that can

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.580
spot said ghosts, and a delivery man who will
somehow save the world.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.680
Plus, Conan O'Brien's in it?

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.400
Honestly, it sounds like a Rick and Morty
episode.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.840
"That hood was threaded by the hand of my
cosplay partner.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:00.260
Wear it, and you too can ride the river rapids
without fear."

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.800
As with any new piece of content that involves
Rick and Morty, the new Death Stranding ad

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.590
serves as a reminder that the long-anticipated
fourth season of Rick and Morty is just around

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:10.080
the corner.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.940
The upcoming season was confirmed in May 2018,
when Adult Swim announced that an additional

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:19.360
70 episodes of the series had been ordered
— likely consisting of seven 10-episode

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:19.860
seasons.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.900
It was another year before it was announced
when Rick and Morty season 4 would debut,

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.400
with the timeframe of November 2019 given.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.661
Then in October 2019, the season's first full
trailer finally arrived... and revealed that

00:03:31.661 --> 00:03:36.180
only five episodes were ready to go starting
in November, with no date given for when the

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.379
second half of season 4 might premiere.

00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:42.790
Now, those first five episodes are nearly
here, and fans will undoubtedly be happy to

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:43.930
take what they can get.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:48.629
The season's first episode, titled "Edge of
Tomorty: Rick Die Rickpeat," is set to debut

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:49.900
on Sunday, November 10.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.480
The episode's title is a play on the Tom Cruise
action film Edge of Tomorrow: Live, Die, Repeat,

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.909
meaning it's possible the series may parody
the film as it parodied Mad Max in season

00:03:59.909 --> 00:04:01.450
3's "Rickmancing the Stone."

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.790
Or maybe the episode will parody a movie that's
nothing like Edge of Tomorrow, since "Rickmancing

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.440
the Stone" had nothing to do with the film
Romancing the Stone.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.240
Who knows!

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:13.520
All we can say for sure about Rick and Morty
season 4 is that we'll be able to watch it

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.120
very soon.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.540
"Lab coat, rip off Doctor Strange."

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.840
Meanwhile, those interested in picking up
Death Stranding can do so when the game launches

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.520
just ahead of Rick and Morty season 4 on Friday,
November 8.

